Action: select_stable  
Action Input: {"k": 7}

Thought: Use inverse-error weighting on the stable pool2 to see if a fitted weighted mean beats the robust median.  
Action: weights_inverse_error  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool2","metric":"rmse","shrinkage":0.0}

Thought: The current best is a robust median over the full pool. A tighter robust pool (pool2) may reduce noise further, so try median over pool2.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool2","rationale":"robust median on the most stable subset"}

Thought: The current best is a robust median on pool2. To see if a fitted weighting can improve, test inverse‑error weights on the same pool.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool2","weights":"w2","rationale":"inverse-error weighting on the stable subset"}

Thought: The ranking is unstable and errors are highly correlated; a forward‑selection weight that adapts per horizon may capture complementary strengths better than a static inverse‑error weight.  
Action: weights_forward  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool2","max_steps":20,"metric":"rmse"}

Thought: The error correlation is very high; pruning redundant models may reduce noise and improve weighted combination.  
Action: prune_redundant  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool_full","corr_threshold":0.95,"metric":"rmse"}

Thought: The current leader uses a robust median on pool2. To see if a weighted approach that shrinks toward uniform could improve, test inverse-error weighting with moderate shrinkage on the same pool.  
Action: weights_inverse_error  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool2","metric":"rmse","shrinkage":0.5,"per_horizon":false}

Thought: Evaluate the forward‑selection weights (w3) on pool2 to see if a Caruana‑style weighted mean beats the current median pool2 leader.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool2","weights":"w3","rationale":"test forward‑selection weights"}

Thought: The ranking is unstable and errors are highly correlated, but the best model changes across horizons. A horizon‑specific one‑hot weighting may capture that shift better than a global weighted mean.  
Action: weights_best_per_horizon  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool2","metric":"rmse"}

Thought: The current best uses median on pool2; try a weighted combination on a pruned, less redundant subset of pool2 to reduce error correlation.  
Action: prune_redundant  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool2","corr_threshold":0.95,"metric":"rmse"}

Thought: The current best is a robust median on pool2. To see if a data‑driven meta‑model weighting can beat it, try a cross‑series meta‑model on the full pool (pool_full) and evaluate.  
Action: weights_meta_model  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool_full","scope":"dataset","metric":"smape","eta":1.0}

Thought: Try pure inverse‑error weighting on the stable pool2 to see if it beats the median baseline.  
Action: weights_inverse_error  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool2","metric":"rmse","shrinkage":0.0,"per_horizon":false}

Thought: Try a very small robust pool (ONLY_DWT_rf + NaiveMovingAverage) with inverse-error weights to see if a minimal, low‑correlation set beats the current median pool2 leader.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool5","weights":"w2","rationale":"minimal robust pool with inverse-error weighting"}

Thought: The current best uses a tiny robust pool with inverse‑error weighting.  To see if a more flexible weighting on a larger stable subset can help, evaluate weighted pool2 with the best‑per‑horizon weights (w5).  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool2","weights":"w5","rationale":"test best‑per‑horizon weights on the stable 7‑model pool"}

Thought: The best validation candidate is already a14, so we accept it as the final strategy.  
Action: accept  
Action Input: {"strategy_id":"a14"}

